{
  "about": [
    "Provenance for the ICC profile bytes and the expected-value data of the F-240 AC15 viewer.colour_frame extension.",
    "The two source profiles are the project-authored synthetic inputs from frozen ICC input tree 81987bd7c13f8e981b62838e18d8afa21b9b7ce4, retained verbatim under inputs/profile-provenance.json of the task inputs. Their entries below are that record's, unedited.",
    "No third-party profile bytes are used, and no product ICC readback is involved: the expected values are hand-vectors computed independently before implementation, from published ICC sRGB D50 colourants, their independently computed inverse, the actual s15Fixed16 profile colourants, ICC.1 curv normalisation and the IEC 61966-2-1 sRGB encoding.",
    "The 16-bit workload's profile is not stored. It is derived at load time from icc_gamma1.icc by rewriting each of the three TRC tags in place: the tag-table size field goes from 14 to 16 and the count-1 u8Fixed8 gamma payload becomes a count-2 table with entries 0 and 65535. The slots are 16 bytes apart, so alignment and every other profile byte are preserved, which the diff regions below record."
  ],
